  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the National TB and Leprosy Control Program in BANGLADESH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to SDG 3 &#x2018;Ensure healthy lives and promote well-being for all at all ages&#x2019; through early case finding, correct management of TB, including MDR-TB, and leprosy and preventive therapy for latent TB infection in the project area is ensured by 2026 maintaining preventive and protective measures for COVID-19. Technical expertise in MDR/RR TB management is developed among the service providers throughout the country.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to SDG 3 &#x2018;Ensure healthy lives and promote well-being for all at all ages&#x2019; through early case finding, correct management of TB, including MDR-TB, and leprosy and preventive therapy for latent TB infection in the project area is ensured by 2026 maintaining preventive and protective measures for COVID-19. Technical expertise in MDR/RR TB management is developed among the service providers throughout the country.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target population is the total population of around 33 million in the 14 districts covered by DF Bangladesh. Specific target groups are the Leprosy and TB assumptive, and patients and their families. Another key population are the garment and other factory workers, mostly women and their children. As to leave no one behind, special attention will also be given to children, elderly people, people with COVID-19 negative testing while having respiratory symptoms, and the diabetic patients.</narrative>
  </description>
